  ],
  "text": "About ten million hectares of forest disappear every year. That is a country, annually. Mostly it is not fire, and not disaster. Mostly it is food. Cattle pasture is the single biggest driver, by a very long way. Then soy. Then palm oil. Then logging. But it is not evenly spread, and it does not only run one way. Brazil cut its rate sharply in some periods. Then it climbed again. And tree cover is genuinely rising across parts of Asia right now. Moralising has never moved these numbers. Policy and price have. Which is worth knowing, because it means the number is not fixed. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
